<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103862" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηνῐκ-αῦτα</span></b> , commoner form for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηνίκα</span>, answering to a Relat., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>at that time, then</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡνίκα . . , τηνικαῦτα . . </span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					7.1.9
				</span></i>
			; answering to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁπηνίκα</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				465
			</span></i>; to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅτε</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅταν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>OC</u>
				393
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OT</u>
				76
			</span></i>, etc.; to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁπότε, ὅκως</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.6.26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.17
			</span></i>; to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεί, ἐπειδάν,
			ἐπειδή</span>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				4.2.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.2.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				21.96
			</span></i>: also with the Art., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ τ</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				1.98
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> without
			a Relat. expressed, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.18
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				63
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				779
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤδη τ</span>. <i>by that
				time</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.51
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.53
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. ἤδη</span> only
			<i>then</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				789
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ τ. ἤδη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					2.150e
				</span></i>
			; <i>at that time</i> of day, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				1.22
			</span></i>; <i>at this hour</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. ἐχθὲς ἔπινον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					<u>Epit.</u>
					166
				</span></i>
			: c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. τοῦ θέρους</span>
			<i>at this lime</i> of the summer, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				1171
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. τοῦ ἔτους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Herod.</u>
					7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> without
			reference to Time, <i>under these circumstances, in this case</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί τ. δρῶμεν</span>; <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				1142
			</span></i> (troch.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				792b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				3.11.14
			</span></i>. (From <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηνίκα</span>, as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνταῦθα</span> from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνθα</span>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
